 "doc": "Plans in call order: 0-1 the generic fBm (seed+3, directions 0.75 p + 0.25 back), 2-3 the street fBm (seed+5, 0.1 p + 0.9 back), then a (worley3, cell_edges) pair for each USED cell diameter (seed + int(d_km), directions 0.85 p + 0.15 back); params.cells_used_km lists them, the fBm ladder is octave_ladder(fine_frequency, fmax) (the plans hold its result). The cells are accumulated in float32 and standardized over the WHOLE array (a global mean and std: the case is one array). 300 scattered float32 directions (the first five are the two poles and the -x, +x, +y axes: the antimeridian is (-1, 0, 0)), 1-D weights. radius 6371, fmax 150: the 15 and 30 km cells are finer than the map resolves (f = 424, 212) and skipped, 60 and 120 km are used. Measured worst difference 2.4e-4 against float64 and 2.9e-4 under a one-ulp nudge: atol 3e-3, rtol 1e-5. Outputs besides `texture` are the intermediates, there to localize a mismatch: generic_std and street_std (the standardized fBm fields), and, when a cell diameter is used, closed_sum and open_sum (the float32 weighted sums of the cell ramps, before standardization) and closed_std / open_std (their standardizations); each has its own measured tolerance, see TEX_INTER in the case module. params.constants holds the mixes, ramps and seed offsets written in the code, and params.cells_per_radian the f = radius_km / d_km compared with fmax for each diameter (`f > fmax` skips, a tie f == fmax is USED; f is computed by a division).",
